WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.800
There are arguably two types of intelligence.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.800
Fluid intelligence is your ability to&nbsp;
reason quickly and independently of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.160
past experiences. It relies on the ability&nbsp;
to hold attention and benefits from a strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.080
working memory. While it can be trained, fluid&nbsp;
intelligence is mainly determined by your genes.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.800
Crystallized intelligence is your ability&nbsp;
to apply knowledge from prior learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.280
that was stored in your long term&nbsp;
memory. It increases with experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.680
and is hence mostly formed by the environment.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:43.840
To solve complex problems, both types&nbsp;
of intelligence need to work together.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.240
To illustrate how fluid and crystallized&nbsp;
intelligence work, let us tell you the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:58.240
of Arthur, a fine young man, who wants to save a&nbsp;
young princess that was captured by an evil witch.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.000
The witch promised to release&nbsp;
the princess only if Arthur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.480
brings her a precious jewel from a secret tomb.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.800
Arthur agrees, begins his quest, and comes&nbsp;
across a deep, dark forest that he must cross.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.200
He navigates through the wilderness with a&nbsp;
compass and a map — using the intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.800
he crystallized when he spent lots&nbsp;
of time studying maps as a boy.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.960
At the end of the forest Arthur&nbsp;
discovers the entrance to the tomb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.240
and sees the prized jewel already&nbsp;
sparkling in the distance.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.920
As he enters the tomb, he&nbsp;
steps on a pressure plate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.240
His crystallized intelligence tells him&nbsp;
that this is a mechanical trap. — something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.320
he learned about earlier in life. He&nbsp;
stands still, and thinks of a solution.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.640
Since he has never been in this situation before,&nbsp;
he cannot draw on past experience. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.880
his fluid intelligence takes over and&nbsp;
allows him to make a new plan on the fly.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.640
Drop the bag! It puts pressure&nbsp;
on the plate and you can grab the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.400
jewel! — crystalized intelligence&nbsp;
takes note for future reference.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.920
Arthur then gave the jewel to the witch, freed&nbsp;
the princess and brought her safely back home.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.600
Suppose Arthur was an average child and we were&nbsp;
to plot the development of his intelligence over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:30.240
90 years. His fluid intelligence would increase&nbsp;
sharply until his early twenties and then peak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:36.160
and decline. His crystallized intelligence would&nbsp;
peak later and slowly decline at a higher age.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:44.880
The psychologist Raymond Cattell coined the terms,&nbsp;
fluid and crystallized intelligence in 1963.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.800
What are your thoughts?
Can you think of a time when you used your fluid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:03:03.840
and when your crystalized intelligence ?&nbsp;
Share your thoughts in the comments below.

